You are given a task to integrate a component from the **kinetik** motion library into this codebase.

# Transition — Ink Blot (`transition-ink-blot`)

Page transition where ink spills from the exact point you clicked: a turbulence-displaced SVG circle grows into a wobbly blot that floods the screen, the page swaps, then the blot drains to the opposite corner.

## What it should do
On click store the pointer position, animate an SVG circle's radius to cover the farthest corner with a displacement filter for ragged edges, swap the page, move the origin to the mirrored point and shrink the radius back to 0.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **svg**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/transition-ink-blot.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Overlay is aria-hidden; nav uses aria-current. Reduced motion swaps instantly.
- **Performance:** One SVG circle with feTurbulence + feDisplacementMap; only r and cx/cy change.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

